{{/* @dot donseba/go-webthings-docs/internal/website.DocsArticleData */}}
<article class="grid max-w-5xl gap-6">
    {{ template "hero.gohtml" . }}

<pre><code>errs := renderer.ValidateForm(&amp;input)
if len(errs) != 0 {
    // Render the same input and errs; do not save it.
}</code></pre>
<table><thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>Tags or controls</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Presence</td><td><code>required:"true"</code>; a string of only spaces counts as empty, except in a password input</td></tr><tr><td>Numbers</td><td><code>min</code>, <code>max</code>, <code>step</code>, for every int, uint and float kind; <code>step</code> counts exactly, from <code>min</code> when there is one</td></tr><tr><td>String length</td><td><code>minLength</code>, <code>maxLength</code>, counted as Unicode characters; <code>minLength</code> does not count spaces at the start and end</td></tr><tr><td>Pattern and content</td><td><code>pattern</code>, <code>prefix</code>, <code>suffix</code>, <code>contains</code>; <code>line:"true"</code> for one line without control characters</td></tr><tr><td>Choices</td><td><code>values</code>, <code>RenderModel.Options</code>, enumerator and mapper allowed values</td></tr><tr><td>Collections</td><td><code>minItems</code>, <code>maxItems</code>, for slice fields and the selected options of a <code>SortedMultiSelect</code></td></tr><tr><td>Email</td><td>Email inputs and <code>email:"true"</code>: a plain address of at most 254 characters, as <code>net/mail</code> parses it; with <code>multiple:"true"</code> a comma-separated list</td></tr><tr><td>URLs</td><td><code>url:"true"</code> (a scheme or an absolute path), <code>url:"http,https"</code> (one of the listed schemes and a host), <code>url:"link"</code> (an http(s) URL, a path, an anchor, a <code>mailto:</code> or <code>tel:</code> address)</td></tr><tr><td>Same value</td><td><code>equal:"Password"</code>, another field of the struct by Go name or <code>name</code> tag</td></tr><tr><td>Files</td><td><code>accept</code>, <code>maxSize</code></td></tr><tr><td>Other checks</td><td><code>bool</code> and <code>zero</code> tags</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>A <code>javascript:</code>, <code>vbscript:</code> or <code>data:</code> URL is never valid, nor a URL with spaces. Rendering an <code>input,url</code> control alone does not enable the server-side URL rule; set a <code>url</code> tag. A float holding <code>NaN</code> or an infinity, and a string that is not valid UTF-8, fail with the rule <code>invalid</code> whatever the other tags. The rules check the value a pointer points to; a nil pointer only fails <code>required</code>.</p>
<p>HTML attributes improve browser feedback, but server-side validation decides whether an input is accepted. <code>ValidEmail</code>, <code>ValidURL</code>, <code>SingleLine</code>, <code>AcceptsFile</code>, <code>ParseSize</code> and <code>OnStep</code> are the same checks in Go, for values that do not come from a form.</p>
<h2>Messages per rule</h2>
<pre><code>Slug string `name:"slug" form:"input,text" label:"Address" required:"true" pattern:"^[a-z0-9-]+$" patternMsg:"Use lowercase letters, digits and dashes"`</code></pre>
<p>Each rule has its own message tag: the rule name followed by <code>Msg</code>, such as <code>requiredMsg</code>, <code>minLengthMsg</code>, <code>patternMsg</code> or <code>valuesMsg</code>. Like labels, these messages are translated, and get the rule’s value when they have a verb for it, such as <code>%d</code>. <code>errorMsg</code> replaces the message of every rule of the field without its own message, and is shown as written. go-form’s own messages show in English when nothing translates them, or in Dutch for a Dutch localizer.</p>
<pre><code>for _, err := range errs {
    if e, ok := err.(form.FieldValidationError); ok &amp;&amp; e.Rule == "required" {
        // …
    }
}</code></pre>
<p>The <code>Rule</code> of a <code>FieldValidationError</code> names the rule that failed, such as <code>required</code>, <code>maxLength</code>, <code>values</code> or <code>invalid</code>, or the name of a custom validator. The errors of a nested struct, named such as <code>address.city</code>, keep their <code>Rule</code>. Messages are for people; <code>Rule</code> is for code that tells errors apart.</p>
<h2>Register a custom validator</h2>
<pre><code>renderer.RegisterValidationMethod("availableName", func(value any, field reflect.StructField) form.FieldErrors {
    name, ok := value.(string)
    if !ok || strings.EqualFold(strings.TrimSpace(name), "admin") {
        return form.FieldErrors{form.FieldValidationError{
            Field: field.Name, Err: "Choose another name.",
        }}
    }
    return nil
})

type Registration struct {
    Name string `name:"name" form:"input,text" label:"Name" validate:"availableName"`
}</code></pre>
<p>The <code>validate</code> tag can contain comma-separated registered names. Return <code>FieldErrors</code> identifying the relevant field; an error that names the Go field is named as the field renders, and gets the validator’s name as its <code>Rule</code>. The renderer places them beside the control. Custom validators run after go-form’s own rules. Keep custom validators configured before serving requests.</p>
<p>The messages of <code>RegisterValidationMethod</code> validators are shown as written. A validator registered with <code>RegisterLocalizedValidation(name, func(value any, field reflect.StructField, loc form.Localizer) form.FieldErrors)</code> gets the localizer, and the form translates the messages it returns; a <code>&lt;name&gt;Msg</code> tag on the field replaces them.</p>
<h2>Application errors</h2>
<p>A <code>FieldError</code> implements <code>FieldError() (field, err string)</code>. <code>FieldValidationError</code> is the provided concrete type; create it with field names, such as <code>form.FieldValidationError{Field: "email", Err: message}</code>. Services can return stable errors that the handler maps to field messages. Cross-field constraints other than <code>equal</code>, and database uniqueness, still belong in application logic.</p>
<p>For localization, use <a href="{{ basePath }}/translations" hx-get="{{ basePath }}/translations" hx-target="#content" hx-push-url="true">ValidateFormLocalized</a> or <code>Bind</code> with a localizer, and a translation callback.</p>
</article>
